   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the banking law, in relation to criteria for the establishment\nof banking development districts",
    "basePrintNo": "S6270",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6270-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [
      {
       "alternate": false,
       "chamber": "SENATE",
       "districtCode": 57,
       "fullName": "George Borrello",
       "imgName": "57_george_borrello.jpg",
       "incumbent": true,
       "memberId": 1370,
       "sessionMemberId": 2006,
       "sessionYear": 2023,
       "shortName": "BORRELLO"
      }
     ],
     "size": 1
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §96-d, Bank L",
    "lawSection": "Banking Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S6270\n\nSPONSOR: SANDERS\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the banking law, in relation to criteria for the estab-\nlishment of banking development districts\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nRequires DFS to consider whether a community is unbanked or underbanked\nwhen establishing Banking Development Districts.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection one: Requires DFS to consider whether a community is unbanked or\nunderbanked when establishing Banking Development Districts, in addition\nto the existing below criteria:\n\n*the location, number, and proximity of sites where banking services are\navailable within the district;\n\n*the identification of consumer needs for banking services within the\ndistrict; *the economic viability and local credit needs of the communi-\nty within the district;\n\n*the existing commercial development within the district;\n\n*the impact additional banking services would have on potential economic\ndevelopment in the district, and\n\n*such other criteria which the superintendent in his or her discretion\nshall identify as appropriate.\n\nSection two: This act shall take effect immediately.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe Banking Development District program, administered by DFS, is a\nprogram designed to encourage the establishment of banks in areas of New\nYork State where there is a need for banking services. The amount of\nunderbanked and unbanked individuals in a particular community is an\nindication of whether a community is in need of banking services.  This\nbill requires DFS consider whether a community is considered unbanked or\nunderbanked when establishing Banking Development Districts.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
